t_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"11.9.10  Switching a relationship copy direction","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":446.53728,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":64.8,"r":357.0130080000005,"t":458.52528},"charspan":[0,48],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/22","text":"11.9.10  Switching a relationship copy direction"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"When a remote copy relationship is in the Consistent synchronized state, the copy direction for the relationship can be changed. Only relationships that are not a member of a Consistency Group, or the only relationship in a Consistency Group, can be switched. In any other case, consider switching the Consistency Group instead.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":387.15885599999996,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":547.1579760000005,"t":432.37128},"charspan":[0,328],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/23","text":"When a remote copy relationship is in the Consistent synchronized state, the copy direction for the relationship can be changed. Only relationships that are not a member of a Consistency Group, or the only relationship in a Consistency Group, can be switched. In any other case, consider switching the Consistency Group instead."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Important: When the copy direction is switched, it is crucial that no outstanding I/O exists to the volume that changes from primary to secondary because all of the I/O is inhibited to that volume when it becomes the secondary. Therefore, careful planning is required before you switch the copy direction for a relationship.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":323.138856,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":142.79999999999995,"r":541.5515879999999,"t":368.35128},"charspan":[0,324],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/24","text":"Important: When the copy direction is switched, it is crucial that no outstanding I/O exists to the volume that changes from primary to secondary because all of the I/O is inhibited to that volume when it becomes the secondary. Therefore, careful planning is required before you switch the copy direction for a relationship."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"To switch the direction of a remote copy relationship, complete the following steps:","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":294.15934799999997,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":501.30014400000044,"t":303.37234799999993},"charspan":[0,84],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/25","text":"To switch the direction of a remote copy relationship, complete the following steps:"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"1.","orig":"1. Open the Copy Services →→ Remote Copy panel.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":276.3229799999999,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":388.39159199999995,"t":289.30085999999994},"charspan":[0,47],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/26","text":"Open the Copy Services →→ Remote Copy panel."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","enumerated":true,"label":"list_item","marker":"2.","orig":"2. Right-click the relationship to be switched and select Switch , as shown in Figure 11-141.","parent":{"$ref":"#/groups/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":260.13997199999994,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.799004,"r":543.9538440000003,"t":269.3529719999999},"charspan":[0,93],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/27","text":"Right-click the relationship to be switched and select Switch , as shown in Figure 11-141."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Figure 11-141   Switching remote copy relationship direction","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":119.697,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":136.8,"r":375.4916999999996,"t":128.02199999999993},"charspan":[0,60],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/28","text":"Figure 11-141   Switching remote copy relationship direction"},{"children":[],"co